  "provider_query": "The first YouTube video, Me at the zoo",
  "answer": "**“Me at the zoo”** is recognized as the first video uploaded to YouTube.\n\n1. **Upload and basics** — Uploaded by co-founder Jawed Karim on April 23, 2005 (around 8:27–8:31 p.m. PDT) to the channel “jawed.” It is about 19 seconds long and remains his only public upload.  \n   Sources: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo), [Jawed Karim – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jawed_Karim), [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw).\n\n2. **What it shows** — Karim stands in front of elephants at the San Diego Zoo and says they have “really, really, really long trunks, and that’s cool.” High-school friend Yakov Lapitsky filmed it.  \n   Sources: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo), [Tubefilter](https://www.tubefilter.com/2025/04/23/20-years-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-2005-jawed-karim/).\n\n3. **Context** — YouTube was started in 2005 by Karim, Chad Hurley, and Steve Chen (former PayPal colleagues). The clip is often described as a simple platform test and an early user-generated / vlog-style video.  \n   Sources: [Apple Scoop](https://applescoop.org/story/history-of-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-to-tv-giant), [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo).\n\n4. **Scale** — View counts reported in recent coverage range from roughly 350 million to over 440 million, with tens of millions of likes. The San Diego Zoo’s pinned comment (“We’re so honored…”) became one of the most-liked comments on the site.  \n   Sources: [YouTube listing](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw), [The Sun](https://www.the-sun.com/tech/14087057/youtube-first-video-me-at-the-zoo-google-karim/), [Wikitubia](https://youtube.fandom.com/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo).\n\n5. **Later use of the description** — Karim has changed the description over the years to comment on YouTube policies (for example, Google+ comment requirements and the removal of public dislike counts).  \n   Sources: [The Sun](https://www.the-sun.com/tech/14087057/youtube-first-video-me-at-the-zoo-google-karim/), [Wikitubia](https://youtube.fandom.com/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo).\n\n6. **Historical status** — Outlets treat it as a milestone of online video and sometimes call it the first YouTube vlog, despite its plain content.  \n   Sources: [Tubefilter](https://www.tubefilter.com/2025/04/23/20-years-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-2005-jawed-karim/), [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo).\n\n7. **Watch it** — Still live at [youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw).",
